Z||000000||8Ball||08-01-2001||05:56 PM||||Have you ever felt like some unseen force was stoping you from your dreams? Well I think That very force is trying to keep me from getting a Fiero. Every single time I get some money saved up so that I can start working on buying a Fiero something goes wrong. Last time I had some money saved up my transmission dropped out of my hyundai. So that set me back a while. This time I had<BR>some saved up and low and behold what has happened???? Well let me see. Axle broke going down the highway at 65, Lost the wheel,<BR>Which snapped the rim and blew the tire. Luckily no major body damage but the front suspension on the drivers side is ruined.<P>I give up.<BR><P>------------------<BR>The Fieroless Fiero Nut||||reg||9
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-01-2001||06:05 PM||||Hey... Don't give up!  <P>If you're looking for a fiero, start small & cheap. I've got an '84 SE that I'll sell just to get you started.  It's black (well, what's left of the body...sun-baked black) It has a nearly new clutch and TO Bearing.  As well as a new starter.  The head has been rebuilt to very high specs (performance built locally).  And the last time I drove it, it ran- mostly.  The rings have some blow-by and the bottom end of the engine needs a rebuild (rings and bearings preferably)... other than that... nevermind.<P>Anyway- not a sales pitch... just don't ever give up, especially when it involves getting a FIERO!  I haven't worked on my '84 'cause I acquired a rough '87 GT and have been working on it ever since (see signature).<P>Good Luck!<BR><P>------------------<BR>________________________<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg"> <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||08-01-2001||06:48 PM||||Oh man I wish I could buy it but one big problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> your sooooo far away.<P>Thanks anyway though I really appreaciate it.<BR>Randy||||reg||1
