Z||000008||8Ball||08-01-2001||11:04 PM||||Maybe a force is trying to keep me out of the hyundai. This is twice in a month or so that almost the exact same thing has happened.<P>   If it wasn't for the fact it is my wife's car, I wouldn't fix it. Gotta keep the spouse happy if I EVER want to have another Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>   I tried to convince my wife that when I put the car on the racks and had to duck the rust falling off (Canadian Car in TN.) that it was time to get rid of it. But alas it is the first car she ever paid for in full by herself. So Gotta keep it on the road it seems.<P>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||08-02-2001||04:49 AM||||Hi Randy, my first fiero was an 87 coupe. Damn thing threw TWO rods at once (at 5500rpm, that is NOT a sound you soon forget...)  Pitty, I kind of liked her. Paid $1900.(and then replaced the #()@&$#*(clutch) I drove her 8kmiles. (getting rid of this one, I won't have time to spend on it and need teh space :(<P>Second fiero was an 88 Formula, silver. Much better car.  Developed a rod knock in all 6 cylenders, currently awaiting total restoration. Paid $2250. I drove her 9kmiles.<BR>Keeping her. Northstar testbed.<P><BR>My latest car is another Formula, but with t-tops!  this one has only 68,000miles on her, and not TWO WEEKS after I got her, my younger brother tailslides into a curb at 45mph...<BR>Fast forward ~6months.<P>She's BACK, and better than ever! All poly all around, with new suspension down to the cradle, and these great 17" wheels and grippy tyres.  Paid $5,000. (plus repairs, and wheels, which were part of repairs.)<P>Someone out there may not want me driving a fiero, but he can GO STUFF IT WHERE THE SUN DOESN'T SHINE!!!! heh :)<P>Overall, you will be MUCH happier spending $~4,000 on a good fiero, than spending $1500 on a beater, and pumping another $3k into her, then still having a beater, albit one that runs.<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000010||8Ball||08-02-2001||12:49 PM||||I know, I can start one of those scams you see in the newspaper all the time.<P>You know the ones that read,<BR>" Make a wish. Send one dollar to P.O. Box whatever. and Your wish will come true."<P>You see that crap in our papers all the time.<BR>Thing is I can't believe people actually fall for it.<P>Some people's kids.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Randy||||reg||1
